# What never belongs in the image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `COPY . .` takes everything in the build context. Without this file that
# includes the test suite, local databases, and every __pycache__ directory
# from the host — none of which the container runs, all of which it pays for
# in image size, and therefore in COLD START TIME.
#
# On a free tier that spins the container down after ~15 minutes idle, boot
# time is not a detail: it is what a visitor waits through on the first
# request. A smaller image is pulled and started faster, every time.

# Local databases. These are the developer's own data and must never ship —
# in production the database is Postgres, and a stray SQLite file next to the
# app is a confusing thing to find.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Secrets. Belt and braces: .env is gitignored, but the build context is the
# working directory, not the git index, so an untracked .env would otherwise
# be copied straight into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests and their caches. The image runs the app; CI runs the tests.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Virtual environments, if one was created in place
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs and git metadata
*.md
.git/
.gitignore
